WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.280
It's official: Marvel Phase Three is here.
So what the heck does that mean? Well, for

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:14.520
one, it means that many of your favorite characters
are about to take a dirt nap. Here's a look

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:20.260
at some of the huge characters that will probably
die in the Marvel Cinematic Universe Phase Three.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.200
Number 1. CAPTAIN AMERICA
No spoilers, but in the comic Captain America:

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.810
Civil War is based on, Captain America gets
killed. Wait, did we say no spoilers? Sorry.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:33.710
But that's not the only reason we don't expect
Cap to make it out of Phase Three alive; while

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.579
star Chris Evans has spoken publicly of his
desire to continue working with Marvel, he's

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:41.260
also been forthright about wanting to work
behind the camera instead of in front of it.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.839
Evans might be around for Phase Four, all
right. He's just more likely to be directing

00:00:44.839 --> 00:00:49.569
Stan Sebastian as the new Captain America.
RIP, Steve Rogers.

00:00:49.569 --> 00:00:52.449
Number 2. THOR
If there's one thing we learned from studying

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:58.109
Norse mythology, it's that Ragnarok is very,
very bad. After all, it involves the destruction

00:00:58.109 --> 00:01:03.749
and death of all the gods. So expecting Thor
to survive the events of Thor: Ragnarok is

00:01:03.749 --> 00:01:08.350
beyond optimistic. There is some hope, though;
in the comics, Ragnarok is an endlessly repeating

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:13.310
cycle of death and rebirth, so it's possible
Thor could be reborn. But he'll have to die

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:17.359
first for that to happen, so don't be surprised
when ol' goldilocks takes a permanent arrow

00:01:17.359 --> 00:01:22.240
to the knee. Or gets reincarnated as a woman, which I would totally be cool with.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.070
Number 3. THANOS
At this point, big cosmic baddie Thanos has

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:30.759
almost had more cameos than Stan Lee. But
in the two-part Avengers: Infinity War, Thanos

00:01:30.759 --> 00:01:35.450
is finally going to get the spotlight—and
it's going to be a bloody one. Thanos, after

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:39.450
all, worships Death. So even when he inevitably
loses, he still gets what he really wants

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.740
most in the end. The question isn't whether
Thanos will die, it's how many heroes he'll

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.420
take down with him. Speaking of which…

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.229
Number 4. IRON MAN
Of all the stars powering the Marvel Cinematic

00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:54.829
Universe, none is as important as Robert Downey
Jr.—and none have been quite so up front

00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:58.649
as Downey about being tired of putting on
his costume again. So it shouldn't come as

00:01:58.649 --> 00:02:03.549
a surprise to anyone if Iron Man makes the
ultimate sacrifice in Avengers: Infinity War,

00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:07.829
especially given the clear foreshadowing of
exactly that in Tony Stark's dream sequence

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:12.440
from Avengers: Age of Ultron. At least it's
probably going to be epic.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.220
Number 5. THE VISION
Tony Stark is just one of many heroes we're

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:19.170
expecting to meet their end in Avengers: Infinity
War. Chances are that The Vision is going

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:23.420
to join him in perpetual rest. Why? Well,
the synthetic man who stole every scene in

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:27.080
Avengers: Age of Ultron was given life by
the Infinity Stone he wears on his brow—and

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.050
Thanos is going to need that stone in order
to complete the Infinity Gauntlet. Hopefully

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:35.660
someone will be able to rebuild Vision after
Thanos dismantles him.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.000
Number 6. DRAX THE DESTROYER
Drax the Destroyer's entire reason for living

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.390
is to exact vengeance on the villains who
killed his family. And that means Thanos.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:46.780
It's inevitable that Drax is going to get
a showdown with Thanos at some point, but

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:50.980
given their relative power levels, it's also
inevitable that Drax is going to come out

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:54.760
on the losing end. Don't be sad, though. When
you think about it, is there really any other

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.380
way the single-minded Drax could go out?

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.200
Number 7. GAMORA
Drax isn't the only member of the Guardians

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.090
of the Galaxy who has a grudge to settle with
Thanos. His adopted daughter Gamora is also

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:08.620
one of many looking to permanently wipe that
giant grin off of Thanos' ugly mug. Given

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:12.630
that he trained her to be the universe's deadliest
assassin, she has a better chance than most.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:17.250
But, like Drax, Gamora has one big thing going
against her odds for survival: in the comics,

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:22.170
they both were killed by Thanos. Hey, it ain't
easy being green.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.060
And at number 8 - EVERYONE
If it sounds like pretty much everyone you

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:30.850
care about is going to die, that's because
they are. In the comic book Infinity Gauntlet,

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:35.290
which all of the cosmic stuff in the Marvel
movies is based on, Thanos actually wins and

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:39.430
kills everyone. Don't be surprised if that's
the cliffhanger ending to Avengers: Infinity

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:43.220
War Part One. Of course, eventually Thanos
is defeated anyway and most of the heroes

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:47.190
are resurrected, so don't worry, the Marvel
Cinematic Universe will survive. Whether you'll

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:51.110
survive the stress of the viewing experience,
though, is another question entirely.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.780
Thanks for watching. Don't forget to like and subscribe if you want more.

